---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 17</p>
  <h1>Technology &amp; <em>devices</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Name the devices on your desk and in your pocket, then learn the small verb chunks that run them: <span class="ex">turn on</span>, <span class="ex">plug in</span>, <span class="ex">charge</span>, <span class="ex">download</span>, <span class="ex">log in</span>. Finish with the survival lines for a bad tech day: <span class="ex">My battery is dead</span> and <span class="ex">The Wi-Fi isn’t working</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">devices + verb chunks</span>
    <span class="tag">turn on · plug in · charge</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read a chat with IT support.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>The small verbs that run your devices.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose, type, and build verb chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe your devices and solve a problem.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Three lines save every bad tech day: <span class="ex">My battery is low</span> (almost empty), <span class="ex">My battery is dead</span> (0 percent), <span class="ex">The Wi-Fi isn’t working</span>. And remember: <span class="ex">text</span>, <span class="ex">call</span>, and <span class="ex">email</span> are verbs too: <span class="ex">I’ll text you.</span></p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has got">has got</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Turn">Turn</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is downloading">is downloading</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="downloads">downloads</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have got">have got</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Turns">Turns</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Wait a minute. The computer <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is downloading" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a big file right now. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 lesson · present continuous)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Turn" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> off your phone, please. The meeting is starting. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 lesson · imperatives)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>My sister <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has got" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a new laptop. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 lesson · have got)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the devices</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Everyday technology at home and at work. Say each one aloud with <span class="ex">I’ve got…</span> or <span class="ex">I use…</span>: <span class="ex">I’ve got a laptop. I use headphones at work.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/laptop.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">laptop</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/phone.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">phone</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/desktop.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">desktop computer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/keyboard.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">keyboard</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/mouse.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">mouse</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/printer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">printer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/television.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">television</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/camera.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">camera</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/video-camera.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">video camera</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/headphones.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">headphones</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/speaker.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">speaker</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/microphone.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">microphone</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/battery.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">battery</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/plug.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">charger</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/signal.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">Wi-Fi signal</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/satellite.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">satellite</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/robot.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">robot</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/video-game.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">game console</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/envelope.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">email</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/globe.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">the internet</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/light.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">light</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Read the chat with IT support</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Support: “Good morning, IT support. How can I help?”</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">You: “My laptop won’t start. The battery is dead, I think.”</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Support: “OK. <strong>Plug in</strong> the charger, wait five minutes, then <strong>turn it on</strong> again.”</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">You: “It’s working now. Thank you!”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">plug in</span> and <span class="ex">turn on</span>. Each verb has a small second word: <span class="ex">in</span>, <span class="ex">on</span>. What do these small words add to the verb?</li>
      <li>The support agent says <span class="ex">turn it on</span>, not <span class="ex">turn on it</span>. Where does <span class="ex">it</span> go?</li>
      <li>You say <span class="ex">The battery is dead</span> and later <span class="ex">It’s working now</span>. Which line describes the problem, and which one describes the fix?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: read the cue, then choose</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Small words change the verb: <b>on</b> starts a device, <b>off</b> stops it, <b>in</b> connects it to power. A battery at 0 percent is <b>dead</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="off">off</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="charge">charge</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="download">download</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="dead">dead</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Turn <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the television. I want to watch the news. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(start it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Turn <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="off" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> your microphone, please. We can hear your dog. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(stop it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Plug <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="in" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the charger, please. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(connect it to power)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>My phone won’t start. The battery is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="dead" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(0 percent · no power)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>I need to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="charge" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> my phone before we leave. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(fill the battery)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>You can <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="download" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the app for free from the store. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(get it from the internet)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: small verbs run your devices</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You don’t need big words to talk about technology. You need <strong>verb chunks</strong>: a short verb plus a small word, or a short verb plus a device. Learn them as complete pieces and say them fast.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>chunk</th><th>use it like this</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>turn on / turn off</b></td><td>Turn on the printer. Turn off your phone. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">start it / stop it</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>plug in / charge</b></td><td>Plug in the charger. Charge your laptop. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">connect it / fill the battery</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>download / install</b></td><td>Download the file. Install the program. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">get it / put it on the device</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>click on / scroll</b></td><td>Click on the link. Scroll down the page. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">press it / move up or down</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>log in / log out</b></td><td>Log in to your account. Log out when you finish. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">enter / leave your account</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>save / delete</b></td><td>Save the document. Delete the old photos. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">keep it / remove it</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>send / receive</b></td><td>Send an email. Receive a reply. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">out / in</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>search for</b></td><td>Search for cheap flights. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">look for information</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The small word can move: <span class="ex">turn on the TV</span> or <span class="ex">turn the TV on</span>. But with <span class="ex">it</span>, the small word always goes last: <span class="ex">turn it on</span>, never <span class="ex">turn on it</span>.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Text</span>, <span class="ex">call</span>, and <span class="ex">email</span> work as verbs: <span class="ex">I’ll text you the address. Call me after work. Email me the report.</span> With <span class="ex">send</span>, the person comes first: <span class="ex">send me the report</span>, not <span class="ex">send to me the report</span>.</li>
      <li>Battery talk: <span class="ex">My battery is low</span> means almost empty; <span class="ex">My battery is dead</span> means 0 percent. For a bad connection, say <span class="ex">The Wi-Fi isn’t working</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Verb + device: say the whole chunk</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Now put the chunks to work. Each sentence below is something people really say at home or in an office: <span class="ex">Please turn off your phone. Can you plug in the charger? Log in to your account.</span> Choose the chunk, then say the full sentence aloud.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the verb chunk</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the whole sentence first. The cue in parentheses tells you the meaning you need.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="turn on">turn on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="turn off">turn off</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="plug in">plug in</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="charge">charge</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="download">download</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="install">install</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="log in">log in</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="search for">search for</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The meeting is starting. Please <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="turn off" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> your phone. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(stop it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I can’t hear you. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="turn on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> your microphone, please. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(it’s off · start it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>My battery is low. Can you <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="plug in" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the charger? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(connect it to power)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>I need to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="charge" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> my laptop before the flight. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(fill the battery)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The report is online. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="download" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the file and save it in your Documents folder. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(get it from the internet)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="install" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the program from the USB drive, then restart the computer. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(put it on the computer)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="log in" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to your account with your email and password. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(enter your account)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>I always <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="search for" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> cheap flights online before I book. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(look for information)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the chunk, then the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type the missing word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">One small word each time: <b>on</b>, <b>off</b>, <b>in</b>, <b>out</b>, or a word from the survival lines. Type it, then say the whole sentence.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The room is dark. Turn <input class="answer-input" data-answer="on" aria-label="answer 1" /> the light. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(start it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The meeting is finished. You can turn <input class="answer-input" data-answer="off" aria-label="answer 2" /> your camera now. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(stop it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The battery is low. Plug <input class="answer-input" data-answer="in" aria-label="answer 3" /> the charger. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(connect it to power)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>You’re on a shared computer, so log <input class="answer-input" data-answer="out" aria-label="answer 4" /> when you finish. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(leave your account)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>My phone won’t turn on. The battery is completely <input class="answer-input" data-answer="dead" aria-label="answer 5" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(0 percent · no power)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I can’t talk now. I’ll <input class="answer-input" data-answer="text" aria-label="answer 6" /> you when I arrive. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(a short phone message · use it as a verb)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="turn off your phone in the meeting">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the office rule</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Your manager has one rule for meetings. Build the instruction, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="phone">phone</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="turn">Turn</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="in">in</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="your">your</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="meeting">meeting</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="off">off</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i need to charge my laptop">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the battery sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Your laptop is at 5 percent and your call starts in an hour. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="charge">charge</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="my">my</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="need">need</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="laptop">laptop</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to me" data-fix="Can you send me the report?" data-why="After send, put the person first, without to: send me the report. You can also say send the report to me, but never send to me the report.">
    <h3>Drill 5: where does the person go?</h3>
    <p>Tap the part that is wrong. With <span class="ex">send</span>, the person comes right after the verb.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="can you">Can you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="send">send</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to me">to me</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the report">the report?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="death" data-fix="My phone is dead." data-why="Death is a noun. For a phone or battery with no power, use the adjective dead: My phone is dead. My battery is dead.">
    <h3>Drill 6: the battery word</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. You need an <strong>adjective</strong> after <span class="ex">is</span>, not a noun.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="my">My</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="phone">phone</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="death">death.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7: say the new sentence, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Say the answer aloud first, in a complete chunk or sentence. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> turn on + the printer &nbsp;→&nbsp; give the instruction</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Turn on the printer.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Turn off the TV. &nbsp;→&nbsp; say it with <em>it</em></p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Turn it off.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> the computer + download a file &nbsp;→&nbsp; what is happening right now?</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The computer is downloading a file.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> My phone is at 0 percent. &nbsp;→&nbsp; say the problem</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>My battery is dead.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> log in &nbsp;→&nbsp; say the opposite</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>log out</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> I’ll call you. &nbsp;→&nbsp; send a written message instead</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I’ll text you.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A chat with IT support</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">IT support: “Hello! How can I help you today?”</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Dana: “Hi. My computer is very slow, and the Wi-Fi isn’t working in meeting room 2.”</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">IT support: “OK. First, save your work and turn off the computer. Wait one minute, then turn it on again. For the Wi-Fi, plug in the white router behind the television and wait for the green light.”</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">Dana: “It’s working now. Thank you!”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood a real IT support chat.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a slow computer and the Wi-Fi">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What are Dana’s two problems?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a slow computer and the Wi-Fi">a slow computer and the Wi-Fi</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a dead battery and the printer">a dead battery and the printer</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the keyboard and the mouse">the keyboard and the mouse</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="save her work">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What should Dana do first?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="save her work">save her work</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="buy a new computer">buy a new computer</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="plug in the router">plug in the router</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="behind the television">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Where is the router?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="behind the television">behind the television</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="next to the printer">next to the printer</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in meeting room 1">in meeting room 1</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your devices:</b> Describe the technology you own and use every day. <span class="ex">I’ve got a laptop, a phone, and wireless headphones. My phone is new, but my laptop is five years old.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Call support:</b> Role-play with the teacher. The teacher is IT support. Explain a problem and follow the instructions. <span class="ex">My laptop won’t start. The battery is dead, I think, and the charger isn’t working.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Help a relative:</b> An older relative has a new phone. Give three simple instructions. <span class="ex">First, turn on the phone. Then click on the green icon. Now scroll down and click on my name.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your screen time:</b> Say how much you use your devices and when. <span class="ex">I check my phone every ten minutes. In the evening I watch videos for an hour, then I turn everything off at eleven.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your internet:</b> Say what you use the internet for, in full sentences. <span class="ex">I use the internet for work emails, maps, and music. I search for recipes, and I download podcasts for the train.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the system</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “To start a device, I turn it ______. To connect it to power, I plug it ______. A battery at 0 percent is ______. To get a file from the internet, I ______ it.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about a device you use every day and one about a tech problem you had this year.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You can name your devices, use the verb chunks that run them, and explain a simple tech problem in real sentences.">
    <h3>Final quiz: choose the right chunk</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="turn off">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. The movie is starting. Please ___ your phone.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="turn off">turn off</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="turn on">turn on</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="plug in">plug in</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="dead">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. My phone won’t turn on at all. The battery is ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="dead">dead</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="low">low</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="full">full</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Plug in">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. ___ the charger. The battery is low.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Plug in">Plug in</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Log in">Log in</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Click on">Click on</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="text">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. I can’t talk now. I’ll ___ you after the meeting.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="text">text</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="texting">texting</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="to text">to text</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Can you send me the report?">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Can you send me the report?">Can you send me the report?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Can you send to me the report?">Can you send to me the report?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Can you send me to the report?">Can you send me to the report?</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="log out">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. You finish work on a shared computer. What do you do?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="log out">log out</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="log in">log in</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="install">install</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="isn’t">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. The Wi-Fi ___ working. I can’t open the page.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="isn’t">isn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="doesn’t">doesn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="aren’t">aren’t</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It’s downloading a file.">
